Task: Cross-adapter parity audit - follow-up correction
Phase: 3 (Framework Adapter Parity)

Caught by the Svelte compiler during the coverage run, not by any test:
  Heelslide.svelte: <g> with a pointerdown/pointermove/pointerup/pointercancel
  handler must have an ARIA role

Self-inflicted: moving role="slider" off the handle left it an unlabelled
element that still responds to pointer events. role="presentation" resolves it
truthfully - the handle is decorative, and every non-pointer route into the
widget goes through the container.

Rejected alternatives: aria-hidden would silence the warning but hide author
children (the reason it was removed a commit earlier); a svelte-ignore comment
would suppress the symptom while leaving the element genuinely unlabelled.

Two assertions expecting no role at all were updated to expect presentation.
Full suite 468 passing, no compiler warnings, tsc and oxlint clean.
